  "notes": "{休|やす}み is a noun meaning rest, break, or vacation (derived from the verb {休|やす}む).\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {休|やす}みを{取|と}る: to take a break/day off\n- {休|やす}みの{日|ひ}: day off\n- {休|やす}みなく: without rest, continuously\n- お{休|やす}みなさい: good night (greeting)\n\nVACATION COMPOUNDS:\n- {夏休|なつやす}み: summer vacation\n- {冬休|ふゆやす}み: winter vacation\n- {春休|はるやす}み: spring break\n- ゴールデンウィーク: Golden Week (late April-early May)\n\nBREAK COMPOUNDS:\n- {昼休|ひるやす}み: lunch break\n- {休憩|きゅうけい}: rest period, intermission\n\nWORD FORMATION:\nNominalized form of {休|やす}む (to rest). Many Japanese nouns are formed by taking the verb stem ({連用形|れんようけい}).",
